# SECTION 01 — PURPOSE

## Purpose

The purpose of Phase-05 is to establish the Technology Landscape for the COREI Institutional Operator Workstation.

Unlike conventional technology selection exercises, Phase-05 does not begin with libraries, frameworks, vendors, or programming languages.

It begins with architecture.

Only after the constitutional, operational, environmental, and behavioural foundations have been established do we determine which technologies are capable of implementing those architectural requirements.

Technology therefore becomes an implementation instrument rather than an architectural driver.

The objective of this phase is to identify, evaluate, validate, and govern every technology that may become part of the COREI Institutional Operator Workstation.

This includes technologies supporting:

* workstation shell,
* layout management,
* docking,
* window management,
* command systems,
* search,
* state management,
* data visualisation,
* charting,
* operational dashboards,
* graph visualisation,
* terminals,
* editors,
* tables,
* AI interaction,
* extension systems,
* collaboration,
* notifications,
* workflow orchestration,
* accessibility,
* performance,
* theming,
* multi-monitor operation.

Every selected technology must strengthen the architecture established throughout Stages 00–04.

No technology shall be introduced merely because it is popular, fashionable, or widely adopted.

