# SECTION 06 — OPERATOR PERSPECTIVE

## Operator Perspective

Professional operators should never notice technology.

They experience professional work.

Technology remains invisible.

Every technology should therefore answer one question.

How does this improve professional operation?

Examples include:

A layout engine should improve:

workspace organisation.

Not demonstrate docking capability.

---

A chart engine should improve:

market understanding.

Not display attractive graphics.

---

A terminal engine should improve:

operational control.

Not terminal emulation itself.

---

A data grid should improve:

institutional investigation.

Not spreadsheet appearance.

---

An AI engine should improve:

professional judgement.

Not conversational novelty.

