I would even recommend that this become a mandatory engineering review process for COREI.

It has an important long-term consequence.

Suppose, five years from now, a new grid library appears that is clearly superior to today's choice.

Most projects face a difficult migration because their architecture has become coupled to the technology.

COREI should not.

Under this model:

The Operator Architecture remains unchanged.
The Operational Environment remains unchanged.
The Experience Architecture remains unchanged.
The Capability Contract remains unchanged.

Only one box changes:

Technology Selection

That is the hallmark of an institutional platform. Technologies are treated as replaceable implementation assets, while the architecture and the institution's way of working remain stable. I believe this principle is one of the strongest safeguards we can build into COREI's long-term evolution.

